# Project Structure and Architecture

This is a Next.js 15 flight booking application with TypeScript, using the App Router architecture.

## Core Technology Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15.1.6 with React 19
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode enabled)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS 4.0
- **State Management**: React Hook Form + Zod validation
- **Data Fetching**: TanStack React Query
- **Package Manager**: pnpm (version 9.1.0)
- **Node Version**: >= 20.0.0
- **UI Components**: Radix UI primitives + custom components

## Project Directory Structure

```
/app                    → Next.js App Router pages and API routes
  /api                  → API route handlers
  /config               → App-level configuration
  /types                → TypeScript type definitions
  /[feature]            → Feature-based page directories

/components             → Reusable React components
  /ui                   → Base UI components (shadcn/ui style)
  /elements             → Custom form elements (Button, TextField, etc.)
  /[FeatureName]        → Feature-specific components (PascalCase)
  /AI-Chat              → Third-party chat UI components

/config                 → Application configuration files
/hooks                  → Custom React hooks
/lib                    → Library code and utilities
/services               → API and storage services
  /api                  → API client services
  /storage              → Browser storage services
/utils                  → Utility functions and helpers
/styles                 → Global styles
/public                 → Static assets
```

## Key Conventions

### Import Paths
- Use `@/` alias for absolute imports from project root
- Example: `import { Button } from "@/components/elements/Button/Button"`

### File Naming
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g., `FlightSearchForm.tsx`)
- Utilities: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `dateUtils.ts`)
- Types: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `flight.ts`)
- API Routes: `route.ts` (Next.js convention)
- Hooks: `useCamelCase.ts` (e.g., `useFlightFormPersistence.ts`)

### Component Organization
- Each major component gets its own directory
- Keep related components together (e.g., FlightCard with its variants)
- Use index files for cleaner imports when appropriate

### Type Definitions
- Define types in `/app/types` for domain models
- Co-locate component-specific types with the component
- Export all types from `/app/types/index.ts` for centralized access

## Configuration Files

- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Dependencies and scripts
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration (strict mode)
- [next.config.ts](mdc:next.config.ts) - Next.js configuration
- [tailwind.config.js](mdc:tailwind.config.js) - Tailwind theme customization
- [eslint.config.mjs](mdc:eslint.config.mjs) - ESLint rules
- [prettier.config.js](mdc:prettier.config.js) - Code formatting rules

## Important Domain Models

- Flight types: [app/types/flight.ts](mdc:app/types/flight.ts)
- Filter types: [app/types/filter.ts](mdc:app/types/filter.ts)

## Testing

- Unit tests: Jest with React Testing Library
- E2E tests: Playwright
- Test files: `*.spec.ts` or `*.test.ts`

## Scripts

- `pnpm dev` - Start development server with Turbopack
- `pnpm build` - Build for production
- `pnpm lint` - Run ESLint
- `pnpm lint:fix` - Auto-fix linting issues
- `pnpm prettier:fix` - Auto-format code
- `pnpm test` - Run Jest tests
- `pnpm e2e:headless` - Run Playwright E2E tests
